{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 26,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.26.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Job answered and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.26.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How hast thou helped ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " without power? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "how",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " savest thou the arm ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that hath",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no strength?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.26.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How hast thou counseled ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him that hath",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no wisdom? and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "how",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hast thou abundantly declared the thing as it is?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.26.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To whom hast thou uttered words? and whose spirit came from thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.26.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Dead ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " are formed from under the waters, and the inhabitants thereof.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.26.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hell ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " naked before him, and destruction hath no covering.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.26.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He stretcheth out the north over the empty place, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hangeth the earth upon nothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.26.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He bindeth up the waters in his thick clouds; and the cloud is not rent under them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.26.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He holdeth back the face of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " throne, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " spreadeth his cloud upon it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.26.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He hath encompassed the waters with bounds, until the day and night come to an end.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.26.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The pillars of heaven tremble and are astonished at his reproof.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.26.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He divideth the sea by his power, and by his understanding he smiteth through the proud.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.26.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By his spirit he hath garnished the heavens; his hand hath formed the crooked serpent.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.26.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lo, these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " parts of his ways: but how little a portion is heard of him? but the thunder of his power who can understand?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
